                  Never tell the user a team was created while that shell is unapproved.
                - with `team.gate: advisory` (or no `agent_teams_plan` mounted) the notice is
                  ADVISORY and says `NO team was staged`: you stage the team yourself at the moment
                  the work warrants one. If the work does not warrant a team (a short or
                  single-threaded task), continue solo and say so in one line.
              The gate is frozen: trigger = explicit flag OR (matchedSignals >= 1), where the explicit
              flag is a `team:` prefix or `!team`, and the soft signals are (B) >=4 distinct
              deliverable verbs, (C) >=3 enumerated steps/action verbs/clauses, (D) an ACTIVE boulder
              work for this workspace (`status: "active"` in .mpd/boulder.json) — a plan FILE alone is
              NOT a signal. The rule is evaluated on the PRE-STEP, BEFORE the sizing doctrine below:
              sizing can add team-shape advice once a team exists or the user asks for one, and it can
